main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member alias template two-parallel-pack expansion: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5 + [temp.alias].  A member alias template
whose body expands two parallel packs (its own pack + the enclosing class's
pack), the shape of libstdc++'s std::tuple _TupleConstraints
(__constructible/__convertible = __and_<is_X<_Types, _UTypes>...>), mis-expands:
the alias's own pack is not bound (the pack passed as the alias's argument list
resolves to zero arguments), so the two-pack body expands against only one pack
and the alias evaluates wrongly.  This is the root cause of cpp17_tuple_basic
(std::make_tuple's forwarding constructor is SFINAE-rejected because
__is_implicitly_constructible<...>() is spuriously false, so the tuple's
element-storing constructor never gets a body).  Flip to CORE once a member
alias template's own pack is bound and a two-parallel-pack body expands in
lock-step.
